+# Narrowing the Veterinarian Directory by Specialty Is In Scope; Free-Text Search and a Page Control Are Not
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+The owner asked on 2026-08-11 for the veterinarian directory to be narrowed to one specialty. Two Non-Goals rows meet in that request, and they have different histories.
+
+NG-9 came out of the 2026-07-31 bootstrap survey. It was derived from the absence of any veterinarian search, not decided at the time — the Non-Goals preamble records that provenance and what it leaves open. Its wording covered every way of narrowing the veterinarian list. Read as written, it barred the request.
+
+NG-10 has no such history. It is declined at intake on 2026-08-11, because the request asks for a request-level contract and says nothing about a visible control.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Read NG-9 as written and refuse the request.** Rejected: that would treat a row derived from absence as a boundary the owner had drawn.
+2. **Build the filter and leave NG-9 as it stands.** Rejected: the row would then contradict a shipped capability, and the boundary would be decided by implication.
+3. **Narrow NG-9 to free-text search** (chosen).
+4. **Build the filter together with a control on the page.** Rejected as wider than the request; deferred rather than refused.
+
+## Decision
+
+The owner states: "Non-goal NG-9 is narrowed: free-text veterinarian search stays out of scope, but filtering the directory by an attribute it already shows is in." This is the first stated decision on NG-9. It narrows a derived row rather than revising a recorded one.
+
+The line NG-9 now draws: typed-in text that searches for a veterinarian is out, and naming one specialty the directory already displays is in. `REQ-VET-003` carries that capability on both veterinarian list surfaces. Both are in scope because the machine-readable list is a supported surface again, stated the same day as `REQ-VET-004`. `REQ-VET-002` stays withdrawn and its id is never reused.
+
+NG-10 declines a form, dropdown, or other page control for choosing the specialty. The owner's stated deferral: "A visible control may come as a follow-up request." Choosing the specialty is a matter of the request alone.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- NG-9 leaves the open provenance consultation narrowed, not confirmed. Whether the rest of the row was ever deliberate stays unknown.
+- NG-10 is the first row the table's framing reason does not explain. Its reason is the deferral recorded here.
+- Free-text veterinarian search needs its own owner decision to enter scope. This request supplies none.
+- A later request for the page control proceeds on its own. This decision neither promises it nor bars it.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-9, NG-10
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed NG-9 row and the new NG-10 row.
+- [`REQ-VET-003`](../prd.md#req-vet-003) — the capability the narrowing admits.
